<Layouts.public flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope}>
  <section class="py-10 text-center sm:py-16">
    <p class="mb-3 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-base-300 bg-base-100 px-3 py-1 text-xs text-base-content/60">
      <span class="inline-block size-1.5 rounded-full" style="background: #0ca30c"></span>
      Built on Elixir and OTP
    </p>

    <h1 class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
      Know a service is down before somebody tells you
    </h1>

    <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-base-content/70">
      PulseOps watches every service you register from its own supervised process, decides when
      something is genuinely broken rather than briefly flaky, and opens an incident on its own.
      Your dashboard updates as it happens.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
      <.link navigate={~p"/users/register"} class="btn btn-primary">
        Start monitoring <.icon name="lucide-arrow-right" class="size-4" />
      </.link>
      <.link navigate={~p"/users/log-in"} class="btn btn-ghost">I already have an account</.link>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="grid gap-4 py-8 sm:grid-cols-3">
    <div class="rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5">
      <span class="flex size-9 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary/10 text-primary">
        <.icon name="lucide-shield-check" class="size-5" />
      </span>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-medium">One process per service</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-base-content/60">
        A service whose endpoint misbehaves cannot affect the monitoring of any other. If its
        process dies, the supervisor replaces it and the rest never notice.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5">
      <span class="flex size-9 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary/10 text-primary">
        <.icon name="lucide-zap" class="size-5" />
      </span>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-medium">Real time, not refreshed</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-base-content/60">
        Status changes are pushed over a WebSocket the moment a monitor sees them. Open the
        network tab: there are no polling requests, because there is no polling.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5">
      <span class="flex size-9 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary/10 text-primary">
        <.icon name="lucide-siren" class="size-5" />
      </span>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-medium">Incidents that close themselves</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-base-content/60">
        Three failed checks open an incident with the reason attached; two good ones resolve it.
        You add the part a monitor cannot know — the root cause.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-8">
    <h2 class="mb-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-base-content/60">
      What happens on every check
    </h2>

    <figure class="flow-diagram rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-4">
      <style>
        .flow-diagram {
          --flow-node: #ffffff;
          --flow-border: #d4d4d8;
          --flow-ink: #18181b;
          --flow-muted: #71717a;
          --flow-edge: #a1a1aa;
          --flow-accent: #7c3aed;
        }
        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
          :root:where(:not([data-theme="light"])) .flow-diagram {
            --flow-node: #27272a;
            --flow-border: #3f3f46;
            --flow-ink: #fafafa;
            --flow-muted: #a1a1aa;
            --flow-edge: #52525b;
            --flow-accent: #a78bfa;
          }
        }
        :root[data-theme="dark"] .flow-diagram {
          --flow-node: #27272a;
          --flow-border: #3f3f46;
          --flow-ink: #fafafa;
          --flow-muted: #a1a1aa;
          --flow-edge: #52525b;
          --flow-accent: #a78bfa;
        }

        /* A travelling dash is what an "animated" edge in a node graph actually
           is. 6 + 8 = 14, so the offset loops seamlessly. */
        .flow-edge {
          fill: none;
          stroke-width: 1.5;
          stroke-dasharray: 6 8;
          animation: flow-dash 1.1s linear infinite;
        }
        @keyframes flow-dash {
          to { stroke-dashoffset: -14; }
        }

        .flow-pulse {
          animation: flow-pulse 2.4s ease-in-out infinite;
        }
        @keyframes flow-pulse {
          0%, 100% { opacity: 0.3; }
          50% { opacity: 1; }
        }

        @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
          .flow-edge, .flow-pulse { animation: none; }
          .flow-edge { stroke-dasharray: none; }
        }
      </style>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <svg
          viewBox="0 0 880 300"
          class="h-auto w-full min-w-[760px]"
          role="img"
          aria-label="A jittered timer starts a supervised task, which probes your endpoint over HTTP. The result comes back to the monitor as a message. Every probe is recorded, and only a change of status opens or resolves an incident and reaches your dashboard."
        >
          <defs>
            <marker
              id="flow-arrow"
              viewBox="0 0 10 10"
              refX="9"
              refY="5"
              markerWidth="5"
              markerHeight="5"
              orient="auto-start-reverse"
            >
              <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="var(--flow-edge)" />
            </marker>
            <marker
              id="flow-arrow-accent"
              viewBox="0 0 10 10"
              refX="9"
              refY="5"
              markerWidth="5"
              markerHeight="5"
              orient="auto-start-reverse"
            >
              <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="var(--flow-accent)" />
            </marker>
          </defs>

          <g stroke="var(--flow-edge)" marker-end="url(#flow-arrow)">
            <path class="flow-edge" d="M184,65 L222,65" />
            <path class="flow-edge" d="M420,65 L458,65" />
            <path class="flow-edge" d="M632,65 L670,65" />
            <path
              class="flow-edge"
              d="M770,94 L770,128 Q770,138 760,138 L568,138 Q558,138 558,148 L558,190"
            />
          </g>

          <%!-- The branch that only fires on a change of status is the one that
                carries colour, because that is the part worth noticing. --%>
          <g stroke="var(--flow-accent)" marker-end="url(#flow-arrow-accent)">
            <path class="flow-edge" d="M464,225 L440,225" />
            <path class="flow-edge" d="M196,225 L168,225" />
          </g>

          <g font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="var(--flow-ink)">
            <g>
              <rect
                x="16"
                y="36"
                width="168"
                height="58"
                rx="10"
                fill="var(--flow-node)"
                stroke="var(--flow-border)"
              />
              <text x="100" y="61" text-anchor="middle">Jittered timer</text>
              <text
                x="100"
                y="79"
                text-anchor="middle"
                font-size="11"
                font-weight="400"
                fill="var(--flow-muted)"
                font-family="ui-monospace, monospace"
              >
                send_after
              </text>
            </g>

            <g>
              <rect
                x="228"
                y="36"
                width="192"
                height="58"
                rx="10"
                fill="var(--flow-node)"
                stroke="var(--flow-border)"
              />
              <text x="324" y="61" text-anchor="middle">Supervised task</text>
              <text
                x="324"
                y="79"
                text-anchor="middle"
                font-size="11"
                font-weight="400"
                fill="var(--flow-muted)"
                font-family="ui-monospace, monospace"
              >
                async_nolink
              </text>
            </g>

            <g>
              <rect
                x="464"
                y="36"
                width="168"
                height="58"
                rx="10"
                fill="var(--flow-node)"
                stroke="var(--flow-border)"
              />
              <circle class="flow-pulse" cx="484" cy="52" r="3.5" fill="var(--flow-accent)" />
              <text x="556" y="61" text-anchor="middle">Your endpoint</text>
              <text
                x="556"
                y="79"
                text-anchor="middle"
                font-size="11"
                font-weight="400"
                fill="var(--flow-muted)"
              >
                one HTTP probe
              </text>
            </g>

            <g>
              <rect
                x="676"
                y="36"
                width="188"
                height="58"
                rx="10"
                fill="var(--flow-node)"
                stroke="var(--flow-border)"
              />
              <text x="770" y="61" text-anchor="middle">Monitor</text>
              <text
                x="770"
                y="79"
                text-anchor="middle"
                font-size="11"
                font-weight="400"
                fill="var(--flow-muted)"
                font-family="ui-monospace, monospace"
              >
                handle_info
              </text>
            </g>

            <g>
              <rect
                x="464"
                y="196"
                width="188"
                height="58"
                rx="10"
                fill="var(--flow-node)"
                stroke="var(--flow-border)"
              />
              <text x="558" y="221" text-anchor="middle">Record the check</text>
              <text
                x="558"
                y="239"
                text-anchor="middle"
                font-size="11"
                font-weight="400"
                fill="var(--flow-muted)"
              >
                every single probe
              </text>
            </g>

            <g>
              <rect
                x="202"
                y="196"
                width="238"
                height="58"
                rx="10"
                fill="var(--flow-node)"
                stroke="var(--flow-accent)"
              />
              <text x="321" y="221" text-anchor="middle">Open or resolve an incident</text>
              <text
                x="321"
                y="239"
                text-anchor="middle"
                font-size="11"
                font-weight="400"
                fill="var(--flow-muted)"
              >
                only when the status changed
              </text>
            </g>

            <g>
              <rect
                x="16"
                y="196"
                width="152"
                height="58"
                rx="10"
                fill="var(--flow-node)"
                stroke="var(--flow-accent)"
              />
              <text x="92" y="221" text-anchor="middle">Your screen</text>
              <text
                x="92"
                y="239"
                text-anchor="middle"
                font-size="11"
                font-weight="400"
                fill="var(--flow-muted)"
              >
                over the socket
              </text>
            </g>
          </g>

          <text x="770" y="120" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="var(--flow-muted)">
            the result arrives as a message
          </text>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-base-content/60">
        The probe never runs inside the process's own callback. A monitor has one mailbox, and a
        request with a five second timeout would block it for five seconds — unable to answer, be
        reconfigured, or shut down cleanly.
      </figcaption>

      <details class="mt-2">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer text-xs text-base-content/50">Read it as steps</summary>
        <ol class="mt-2 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-base-content/70">
          <li>A timer fires, spread by up to 10% so monitors never probe in lockstep.</li>
          <li>The probe runs in a supervised task, off the monitor's own callback.</li>
          <li>Your endpoint answers, times out, or refuses the connection.</li>
          <li>The outcome reaches the monitor as an ordinary message.</li>
          <li>Every probe is recorded, whatever it said.</li>
          <li>Three failures open an incident; two successes resolve it.</li>
          <li>A change — and only a change — is broadcast to every open dashboard.</li>
        </ol>
      </details>
    </figure>
  </section>
</Layouts.public>
